      "text": "Day 20: Authentication setup with redux:\nToday i learnt redux wiht authentication setup. i create\nredux store using configurStore and inside pass object\nas a reducer: { auth: authReducer} and and create\nauthSlice.jsx inside authSlice created using createSlice()\ninside createSlice pass object this is code of authSlice\n\ntimport { createSlice } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\n\nconst authSlice = createSlice({\n    name: \"auth\", \n    initialState: {\n        user: null,\n        isAuthentication: false,\n    },\n    reducers: {\n        addUser: (state, action) => {\n            state.user = action.payload\n            state.isAuthentication = true\n        },\n        removeUser: (state) => {\n            state.user = null\n        }\n    }\n});\n\nexport const {addUser, removeUser} = authSlice.actions;\nexport default authSlice.reducer;\n\n\nafter that created three pages homepage, loginpage and \nregister page also i create custom hook for login and register\nfunctionality, and use that authHook data into loginpage and\nregisterpage. \ni used react-router for routing auth layout and main layout.\ni wrap auth layout to publicProtecte.jsx and wrap mainLayout\nusing mainProtected.jsx \nwhen user logged success full then they can't can't again authLayout\nwithout logout and when user not logged then can't go on mainLayout\n\non AuthHook.jsx I wrote logic of login and registration. then i used \ndispatch for call addUser action and pass user when user login.\nand also I used useSelector in publicprotected and mainprotected\nfor checking user is logged or not for proteaction mainlayout or\nauthlayout. also i used redux hook useNavigate() for performation \nrouting on go to different pages. authlayout to mainlayout and \nmainloyout to authlayout. \n \n\n                 ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Day 20: Authentication setup with redux:\nToday i learnt redux wiht authentication setup. i create\nredux store using configurStore and inside pass object\nas a reducer: { auth: authReducer} and and create\nauthSlice.jsx inside authSlice created using createSlice()\ninside createSlice pass object this is code of authSlice\n\ntimport { createSlice } from \"@reduxjs/toolkit\";\n\nconst authSlice = createSlice({\n    name: \"auth\", \n    initialState: {\n        user: null,\n        isAuthentication: false,\n    },\n    reducers: {\n        addUser: (state, action) => {\n            state.user = action.payload\n            state.isAuthentication = true\n        },\n        removeUser: (state) => {\n            state.user = null\n        }\n    }\n});\n\nexport const {addUser, removeUser} = authSlice.actions;\nexport default authSlice.reducer;\n\n\nafter that created three pages homepage, loginpage and \nregister page also i create custom hook for login and register\nfunctionality, and use that authHook data into loginpage and\nregisterpage. \ni used react-router for routing auth layout and main layout.\ni wrap auth layout to publicProtecte.jsx and wrap mainLayout\nusing mainProtected.jsx \nwhen user logged success full then they can't can't again authLayout\nwithout logout and when user not logged then can't go on mainLayout\n\non AuthHook.jsx I wrote logic of login and registration. then i used \ndispatch for call addUser action and pass user when user login.\nand also I used useSelector in publicprotected and mainprotected\nfor checking user is logged or not for proteaction mainlayout or\nauthlayout. also i used redux hook useNavigate() for performation \nrouting on go to different pages. authlayout to mainlayout and \nmainloyout to authlayout. \n \n\n                 ",
